# Supabase project — copy to .env and fill in
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# PostHog — project API key is publishable (like the Supabase anon key). Host
# is https://us.i.posthog.com or https://eu.i.posthog.com. Leave unset to
# disable capture. Privacy rules live in src/lib/posthog.ts (D-114).
# VITE_POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN=phc_...
# VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# Sign in with Apple. Native iOS always offers it (App Store guideline 4.8 —
# offering Google forfeits the "own account system only" exemption). The WEB /
# desktop redirect path needs a Services ID + key in Supabase, which the client
# cannot detect, so it is declared here. Leave unset and the web shows exactly
# Google + email code, as before. Full runbook: docs/apple-sign-in.md.
# VITE_APPLE_AUTH=1
#
# Server (supabase secrets) — required for account deletion to revoke Apple's
# grant via /auth/revoke, which guideline 5.1.1(v) makes its own rejection
# reason. APPLE_SIWA_CLIENT_ID defaults to APPLE_BUNDLE_ID (correct for native).
# APPLE_SIWA_TEAM_ID=ABCDE12345
# APPLE_SIWA_KEY_ID=ABC123DEFG
# APPLE_SIWA_PRIVATE_KEY=-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----
# APPLE_SIWA_CLIENT_ID=day.nuvo.app

# Optional — DEV ONLY password auto-login. The UI offers Google, Apple (iOS /
# VITE_APPLE_AUTH) and an email code; this only works if the user still has an
# email identity. Prefer staying signed in, or clear these and use Continue
# with Google. Put real values in .env.local.
# Tree-shaken out of every production build.
# VITE_DEV_EMAIL=you@example.com
# VITE_DEV_PASSWORD=your-password

# Resend — server-only (Supabase secrets). Outbound: stripe-webhook referral
# mail. Inbound: `inbound-email` (email → inbox task). Not Vite env except the
# domain the SPA prints in Settings (must match the receiving domain).
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# RESEND_FROM=Nuvo <hello@nuvo.day>
# RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# INBOUND_MAIL_DOMAIN=inbox.nuvo.day
# VITE_INBOUND_MAIL_DOMAIN=inbox.nuvo.day

# iOS App Store IAP — StoreKit Product ID strings (not prices, not Apple IDs).
# Connect group Nuvo Pro 22327993 (not submitted, no intro offer).
# Monthly Apple ID 6804259519 · Annual Apple ID 6804258767 — Connect-internal only.
# Product IDs passed to product() are these strings:
# VITE_NUVO_IAP_MONTHLY=NUVO_IAP_MONTHLY
# VITE_NUVO_IAP_ANNUAL=NUVO_IAP_ANNUAL
# These two are PLAIN VALUES, not secrets, and the "Build signed IPA" step of
# .github/workflows/ios-release.yml must set them — Vite only bakes VITE_* vars
# that exist at build time. Left unset, the paywall would have no catalog, so
# configuredIapProductIds() falls back to the same two strings; the fallback is
# the net, the workflow is the contract. tests/iap-catalog-env.test.ts holds both.
# Server (supabase secrets): same values. Trial is app-side trial_ends_at.
